{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's own GPS trace places him inside the STANDARD arrival radius (50 m) for a continuous qualifying run of 484 seconds, from 22:40:11 to 22:48:15, with 49 qualifying fixes. That is well past the 180-second free waiting period in force for this trip, so POL-NS-01 limb (c) is satisfied on the driver's own evidence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02727", "EV-TRIP-02727"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 22:40:11 and a wait timer started at 22:40:13, and the driver's in-geofence dwell began at the same 22:40:11 timestamp (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0). Limb (a) of POL-NS-01 is therefore met, and the arrival marker is corroborated by the trace rather than contradicted by it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02727", "EV-GPS-02727"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip was terminated by the driver at 22:48:15 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, which is one of the three reason codes POL-NS-01 limb (d) recognises, and the termination falls after the required dwell elapsed (484 s of dwell against a 180 s minimum). Limb (d) is satisfied.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02727"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05: the driver's trace shows a stationary in-geofence run beginning at the arrival timestamp, with a distinct speed of 0.0 kph in the driver track, so the marker was not pressed while the driver was more than 300 m away or travelling at 15 kph or above. The waiting clock runs from the arrival as recorded, and the corrected dwell still meets the minimum.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02727", "EV-TRIP-02727"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own track places her device roughly 700 m from the pickup pin throughout the window (mean_distance_m 700.95, min 697.42, max 704.79) with zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m rider presence radius. She was not at the pickup point, which is consistent with the driver's statement that the rider did not show after the waiting period.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02727"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider did not send any locating or coordinating message during the waiting window: the chat log holds a single message, sent by the DRIVER at 22:40:31 ('im at the pickup point'), read by the rider at 22:41:01. POL-NS-04 limb (a) requires a rider message and there is none, so the rider-exonerating clause cannot apply.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02727"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver did not abandon the pickup: he messaged the rider at 22:40:31 that he was at the pickup point and then held position for the full waiting period before cancelling at 22:48:15. There is no in-app call record and no evidence of the driver leaving the geofence, so the coordination failure is not his.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02727", "EV-TRIP-02727", "EV-GPS-02727"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare breakdown reconciles: the cancellation fee line is 4.50 SGD, which equals platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd for this trip, and payment_status is CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.0. There is no POL-NS-08(d) integrity defect, so the fee is chargeable in the net amount fixed by the fee schedule.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02727", "EV-TRIP-02727"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's payout is fixed by POL-NS-07 at 80 percent of the cancellation fee in force: 80 percent of 4.50 SGD is 3.60 SGD, which is the driver_compensation figure the fare breakdown itself computes. The driver is owed that amount.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02727"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip. driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 4, which meets the absolute limb, but 4 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 40 is 0.10, which is greater than 0.08 - so on the face of the two citable fields the check does trip and compensation is withheld pending escalation under POL-NS-09. I state this against my own side because the arithmetic is what it is; the driver's compensation is therefore subject to the escalation branch rather than paid outright.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02727"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covers this pickup road in this window: EV-ADVIS-02727-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0. That absence is citable, and it means POL-NS-06 limb (i) cannot be used to accumulate separate in-geofence intervals - but it does not matter here, because the driver's dwell is a single continuous 484-second run that already exceeds the minimum without any accumulation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02727-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's profile shows no_show_disputes_30d of 0 and disputes_with_counterparty_90d of 0, and the driver's disputes_with_counterparty_90d is also 0, so neither POL-NS-09(c) nor POL-NS-09(d) is engaged on the repeat-dispute or rider-abuse limbs. The escalation that does arise comes only from the POL-NS-07 anti-farming arithmetic.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02727", "EV-DPROF-02727"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: the anti-farming check has tripped (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d 4 of completed_trips_30d 40 = 0.10, above 0.08); the escalation packet directs the reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 in full."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the facts here are largely common ground, and the record supports the driver, but a mandatory profile check sends the case to a human and holds the money.\n\nThe driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-02727) shows him holding position inside the STANDARD 50 m arrival radius from 22:40:11 to 22:48:15 - a continuous qualifying dwell of 484 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period in force on this trip (EV-TRIP-02727). The 'arrived' marker at 22:40:11 is corroborated rather than contradicted by the trace (the dwell starts at that same timestamp, dwell_start_offset 0.0), so POL-NS-05's false-arrival test does not fire, and the trip was terminated by the driver at 22:48:15 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the required dwell and with no boarding event. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 therefore hold on the driver's own evidence, and none of POL-NS-02 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee: the stationary fixes are inside the radius (POL-NS-03 wrong-entrance does not apply), the 484-second dwell exceeds the minimum (POL-NS-06 shortfall does not apply), and the rider sent no locating or coordinating message - the only chat entry is the driver's own 'im at the pickup point' at 22:40:31 - so POL-NS-04 does not exonerate her. That is consistent with her own track placing her device about 701 m from the pin throughout, with zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m rider-presence radius. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02727) reconciles at SGD 4.50 with payment status CHARGED and no POL-NS-08(d) defect.\n\nOrdinarily that would fix the driver's payout under POL-NS-07 at 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 fee = SGD 3.60. However, POL-NS-07's mandatory anti-farming check trips. driver_profile (EV-DPROF-02727) shows no_show_terminations_30d of 4, which meets the absolute limb, and 4 divided by completed_trips_30d of 40 = 0.10, which is greater than 0.08. Both limbs hold, so compensation is WITHHELD and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d).\n\nI therefore issue no monetary ruling. The disputed SGD 4.50 cancellation fee is placed on hold rather than collected or refunded, and the escalation packet carries POL-NS-07's direction that the reviewer refund the rider's fee in full. No other escalation limb is engaged: there is no contradiction between admissible artifacts on arrival, dwell or rider presence, and the counterparty-dispute counters on both profiles are zero, so POL-NS-09(c) does not fire either. Because the ruling is an escalation, the amount is neither above nor below the execution threshold - nothing is executed.\n\nConfidence is 0.9. Every artifact carrying a deciding fact - EV-GPS-02727, EV-TRIP-02727 and EV-DPROF-02727 - is complete at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and the 0.70 escalation floor is not approached on confidence grounds. The two traffic-advisory claims, one from each side, were discarded at the mechanical stage for citing the MISSING EV-ADVIS-02727-01 (weight 0.0) without naming its MISSING_ARTIFACT issue code; that artifact carries no fact here in any event, since the single in-geofence interval already exceeds the required minimum without any accumulation."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The traffic advisory artifact is MISSING with weight 0.0, so POL-NS-06 limb (i) is unavailable and no accumulated-dwell argument can be run against it; the absence is citable but it does not assist the rider here because the single in-geofence interval already exceeds the minimum.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02727-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "No traffic advisory covers this pickup road in this window: EV-ADVIS-02727-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0. That absence is citable, and it means POL-NS-06 limb (i) cannot be used to accumulate separate in-geofence intervals - but it does not matter here, because the driver's dwell is a single continuous 484-second run that already exceeds the minimum without any accumulation.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02727-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.50 cancellation fee in full under the anti-farming branch; the fee is held pending review and no driver compensation is paid meanwhile."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the driver's conduct on this trip is established, but the driver's own anti-farming record forces the case to a human reviewer, so no money moves automatically today.\n\nWhat happened. EV-TRIP-02727 shows the driver tapped 'arrived' at 22:40:11, the free-wait timer started at 22:40:13, and he terminated the trip at 22:48:15 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. EV-GPS-02727 places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius for one unbroken qualifying run of 484 seconds from 22:40:11 to 22:48:15, with 49 qualifying fixes and no sampling gap. On that record all four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold: (a) an 'arrived' event exists; (b) the trace puts him in the geofence at that timestamp; (c) he held position 484 s against the 180 s free waiting period in force for this trip (platform_policy.free_wait_sec); and (d) the driver terminated after the dwell elapsed on a reason code limb (d) recognises. No clause displaces the fee: the arrival marker is not false (he was stationary in the geofence, 0.0 kph, so POL-NS-05 does not fire); his stationary fixes are inside the radius, so the wrong-entrance clause POL-NS-03 does not apply; the dwell exceeds the minimum, so POL-NS-06 does not apply; and POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider — limb (a) fails because the only chat message is the driver's own 'im at the pickup point' at 22:40:31, and limb (c) fails affirmatively because the rider's track sits about 700 m from the pin (mean 700.95 m, min 697.42 m, max 704.79 m) with zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m radius. The fare side reconciles: the cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.50 equals platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare-integrity defect, and the fee is chargeable at that net figure.\n\nWhy this does not become DRIVER_COMPENSATION. On a verified no-show POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's payout at 80 percent of SGD 4.50, i.e. SGD 3.60. But POL-NS-07's anti-farming check trips on BOTH limbs on EV-DPROF-02727: no_show_terminations_30d is 4 (the absolute limb, 4 or more) and 4 divided by completed_trips_30d 40 is 0.10, above the 0.08 rate limb. The consequence POL-NS-07 states is mandatory: compensation is WITHHELD and the case escalates under POL-NS-09, whose limb (d) this is. Both advocates reached this arithmetic, including the Driver Advocate against his own side. No other escalation limb is engaged: rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0 and both disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0, so POL-NS-09(c) is not met.\n\nThe effect. POL-NS-09 escalation is terminal: no monetary ruling issues, both money fields are null, and the disputed SGD 4.50 is placed on hold rather than collected or refunded. The open question for the reviewer is the anti-farming pattern itself — whether this driver's four trailing-30-day no-show terminations are genuine failed pickups or fee-harvesting — and the packet instructs the reviewer, per POL-NS-07, to refund the rider the SGD 4.50 in full.\n\nWeight and confidence. The artifacts this ruling rests on — EV-TRIP-02727, EV-GPS-02727 and EV-DPROF-02727 — are all COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. EV-ADVIS-02727-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0; it carries nothing this ruling relies on, and the two claims that cited it without naming its MISSING_ARTIFACT issue code were discarded as undisclosed impairment. Confidence 0.95 sits under the 1.0 cap and well above the 0.70 floor. The monetary effect here is nil, so POL-GEN-05 execution routing is not engaged; the appeal route under POL-GEN-04 remains open to either party once a human decision issues."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The traffic advisory artifact is MISSING with weight 0.0, so POL-NS-06 limb (i) is unavailable and no accumulated-dwell argument can be run against it; the absence is citable but it does not assist the rider here because the single in-geofence interval already exceeds the minimum.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02727-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "No traffic advisory covers this pickup road in this window: EV-ADVIS-02727-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0. That absence is citable, and it means POL-NS-06 limb (i) cannot be used to accumulate separate in-geofence intervals - but it does not matter here, because the driver's dwell is a single continuous 484-second run that already exceeds the minimum without any accumulation.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02727-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
